### ====================================================================
### Module 05: Application Integration - Card Dispute & Chargeback Engine
### Interactive REST Client Test Scenarios
### ====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@apiKey = sk_live_card_disputes_test_key_001
@contentType = application/json

### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. System Health & Readiness Check
### --------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name healthCheck
GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}

### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Happy Path Workflow: Dispute Submission & Polling
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Step A: Submit a new Card Dispute
# NOTE: Pre-creates database record with status="processing" before Celery dispatch (anti-blackhole contract).
# @name submitDispute
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
    "transaction_id": "tx_req_rest_happy_001",
    "card_token": "tok_card_9921_sec",
    "card_last_four": "4242",
    "amount": "149.99",
    "currency": "USD",
    "reason": "fraudulent",
    "evidence_notes": "Cardholder confirmed card was in possession; merchant unrecognized."
}

### Step B: Inspect Immediate In-Flight State (Anti-Blackhole Contract)
# NOTE: Immediate query returns HTTP 200 OK with in-flight status: "processing" (zero-404 guarantee).
# @name getDisputeImmediate
GET {{baseUrl}}/disputes/{{submitDispute.response.body.id}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Step C: Poll Terminal Status After Worker Transmission
# NOTE: Once Celery worker transmits evidence to clearinghouse, status transitions to "submitted_to_network".
# @name getDisputeFinal
GET {{baseUrl}}/disputes/{{submitDispute.response.body.id}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Idempotency Verification Workflow
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Attempt duplicate dispute submission for the same transaction_id (Expected: HTTP 409 Conflict)
# @name submitDuplicate
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
    "transaction_id": "tx_req_rest_happy_001",
    "card_token": "tok_card_9921_sec",
    "card_last_four": "4242",
    "amount": "149.99",
    "currency": "USD",
    "reason": "duplicate",
    "evidence_notes": "Duplicate submission attempt."
}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. In-Flight Cooperative Cancellation Workflow
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Step A: Submit a Dispute Destined for Cancellation
# @name submitForCancel
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
    "transaction_id": "tx_req_rest_cancel_002",
    "card_token": "tok_card_8812_sec",
    "card_last_four": "1234",
    "amount": "45.00",
    "currency": "USD",
    "reason": "unrecognized",
    "evidence_notes": "Initiated cancellation prior to clearinghouse network transmission."
}

### Step B: Cancel Dispute In-Flight (Revokes Celery Task via SIGTERM)
# @name cancelDispute
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes/{{submitForCancel.response.body.id}}/cancel HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Step C: Attempt Second Cancellation on Cancelled Dispute (Expected: HTTP 409 Conflict)
# @name cancelDisputeDuplicate
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes/{{submitForCancel.response.body.id}}/cancel HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Clearinghouse Failure Simulation & Manual Retry Workflow
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Step A: Submit Dispute with Simulated Clearinghouse Failure (?simulate_failure=true)
# @name submitSimulateFailure
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes?simulate_failure=true HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
    "transaction_id": "tx_req_rest_fail_003",
    "card_token": "tok_card_7733_sec",
    "card_last_four": "5678",
    "amount": "250.00",
    "currency": "USD",
    "reason": "goods_not_received",
    "evidence_notes": "Package not delivered; simulating clearinghouse network timeout."
}

### Step B: Poll Until Dispute Reaches 'failed' State
# @name getFailedDispute
GET {{baseUrl}}/disputes/{{submitSimulateFailure.response.body.id}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Step C: Retry Failed Dispute (Increments attempt_count and re-enqueues)
# @name retryFailedDispute
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes/{{submitSimulateFailure.response.body.id}}/retry HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Step D: Attempt Retry on Non-Failed Dispute (Expected: HTTP 409 Conflict)
# @name retryNonFailedDispute
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes/{{submitDispute.response.body.id}}/retry HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Security, Authentication & Validation Scenarios
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Scenario A: Missing API Key (Expected: HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
# @name authMissingKey
GET {{baseUrl}}/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}

### Scenario B: Invalid API Key (Expected: HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
# @name authInvalidKey
GET {{baseUrl}}/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: sk_invalid_key_99999999

### Scenario C: Non-Existent Dispute UUID (Expected: HTTP 404 Not Found)
# @name nonExistentDispute
GET {{baseUrl}}/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 HTTP/1.1
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Scenario D: Invalid Dispute Payload - Validation Failure (Expected: HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity)
# @name invalidPayload
POST {{baseUrl}}/disputes HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
    "transaction_id": "tx",
    "card_token": "short",
    "card_last_four": "abc",
    "amount": "-10.00",
    "currency": "INVALID",
    "reason": "unsupported_reason"
}
